  "answer_text": "Where you should order a birthday cake online depends on whether you want a famous bakery cake shipped nationwide, a local same-day delivery, or an international shipment. \n\n---\n\n### 1. Nationwide US Shipping (Shipped Frozen to Your Door)\nIf you want a spectacular, high-quality cake shipped from a famous bakery anywhere in the United States, these are the top options:\n\n*   **Goldbelly:** This is the ultimate online marketplace for food. You can order legendary cakes from famous bakeries across the country (like Duff Goldman\u2019s Charm City Cakes, NYC\u2019s Veniero's, or Carousel Cakes) and have them shipped directly to your door.\n*   **Milk Bar:** Famous for its iconic, colorful, \"naked-style\" **Birthday Cake** (a modern spin on classic funfetti), as well as cake truffles and gluten-free options. They ship nationwide, and the cakes arrive frozen to preserve freshness.\n*   **Magnolia Bakery:** Known for classic NYC-style baked goods, you can order their traditional vanilla or chocolate birthday cakes\u2014as well as their world-famous banana pudding\u2014shipped nationwide.\n*   **Caroline\u2019s Cakes:** Based in South Carolina, they are famous for traditional Southern layer cakes, including their legendary 7-Layer Caramel Cake, which can be ordered with festive birthday sprinkles.\n*   **Harry & David:** Perfect for gifting, they offer elegant gourmet chocolate cakes, classic celebration cakes, and even creamy cheesecakes sourced from *The Cheesecake Factory*. \n\n---\n\n### 2. Local & Same-Day Delivery (US)\nIf you need a cake delivered **today or tomorrow**, shipping nationwide won't work. Instead, try these local services:\n\n*   **Nothing Bundt Cakes:** With hundreds of locations across the US, you can order their extremely moist, signature bundt cakes (like Red Velvet or Confetti) decorated specifically for birthdays online for local pickup or hand-delivery.\n*   **On-Demand Delivery Apps (Instacart, DoorDash, Uber Eats):** You can use these apps to order same-day cakes from local grocery store bakeries (like Whole Foods, Publix, or Safeway) or from independent bakeries in your immediate area. \n*   **Local Bakeries via Google Maps or Yelp:** Search for \"custom birthday cakes near me.\" Most local bakeries now have online ordering systems on their websites where you can customize flavors, sizes, and writing, and arrange for curbside pickup or local courier delivery.\n\n---\n\n### 3. International Cake Delivery\nIf you are ordering a cake to be delivered outside the US, or if you live abroad and want to send a cake to someone in another country:\n\n*   **In the UK:** \n    *   **Lola\u2019s Cupcakes:** Offers gorgeous, handcrafted birthday cakes (including highly-rated red velvet and vegan options) delivered across London and the UK.\n    *   **Patisserie Valerie:** Known for handmade, luxury birthday cakes with next-day UK delivery. \n    *   **Cutter & Squidge:** Highly popular for unique \"all-natural\" cake designs and delicious flavor options.\n*   **Global / Multi-Country Delivery:**\n    *   **FNP (Ferns N Petals) & TheGiftPortal:** Excellent international networks that allow you to order cakes online in one country and have them freshly baked and delivered by a local partner bakery in the US, India, UAE, and dozens of other countries.\n    *   **Cyber-Florist or RussianFlora:** These services specialize in international gift and cake deliveries, making it easy to send a birthday cake paired with flowers or chocolates across Europe, Asia, and the Americas using international credit cards.\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Quick Tips for Ordering Online:\n1.  **Lead Time:** Nationwide shipped cakes are sent frozen with dry ice. You will need to order them **2 to 4 days in advance** so they have time to ship and thaw in your refrigerator before the party.\n2.  **Dietary Restrictions:** If you need gluten-free, vegan, or nut-free cakes, **Milk Bar** (gluten-free options) or local specialty bakeries 